<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21204" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hypocrĭta</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-es</span></b> , ae,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποκριτής</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A mime who accompanied the delivery of an actor by
				gestures</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 2,
				17, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 3,
				7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In eccl. Lat., <i>a hypocrite</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Vulg. Job, 8, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Matt. 6,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Luc. 12, 56 al.</span></i></div>
